e refunds may be blocked by policy and require human approval: if the result says escalation is required, do NOT retry — call escalate_to_human with the order details instead.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"order_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Exact order ID, e.g. 'ORD-10421'.", "pattern": "^ORD-\\d{5}$"}, "amount": {"type": "number", "description": "Refund amount in USD. Omit for a full refund.", "exclusiveMinimum": 0}, "reason": {"type": "string", "description": "Why the refund is being issued.", "enum": ["damaged", "not_received", "wrong_item", "changed_mind", "other"]}}, "required": ["order_id", "reason"]}}, {"name": "escalate_to_human", "description": "Hand the case to a human support agent. Use when: a refund is blocked by policy and needs approval; the customer explicitly asks for a human; the request needs a policy exception; or tools keep failing with non-retryable errors. The human has NOT seen this conversation, so `summary` must stand alone: (1) what the customer wants, (2) facts you verified (order status, total, dates), (3) actions already taken or blocked. State facts only — do not speculate about fraud or the customer's honesty. After escalating, tell the customer a human will follow up; never say the issue is resolved.", "input_schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"reason_category": {"type": "string", "description": "Primary reason for escalating.", "enum": ["refund_over_limit", "customer_requested_human", "policy_exception", "tool_failure", "other"]}, "summary": {"type": "string", "description": "Standalone handoff note: request, verified facts, actions taken/blocked."}, "order_id": {"type": "string", "description": "Related order ID, if any.", "pattern": "^ORD-\\d{5}$"}, "customer_email": {"type": "string", "description": "Customer's email, if known.", "format": "email"}, "requested_amount": {"type": "number", "description": "Refund amount (USD) the customer wants, if applicable.", "exclusiveMinimum": 0}}, "required": ["reason_category", "summary"]}}]
